# Cap cluster 5: a mixed mass of eight caps with a small glowing dome, 8 caps of several kinds grown into one soft mass on short stout stems, about 9 m across and 7 m tall.
# Drawn instanced behind the hills' crest, seen from 30 m and more, so it needs no detail finer than its caps. Its stems reach 1.5 m
# below its base, so it stands on a slope without showing its foot. The fungal counterpart of the meadow's crest clusters.
format 1
collider capsule

# Fewer vertices than its size would give it: a big, simple form seen from far away
Detail detail=0.25
    Intersection
        Translate translation=(0, 10, 0)
            Box size=(7, 11.5, 7)
        SmoothUnion smoothness=0.25
            Material material=ftree_stem
